; parity.exe compares the rasterizing rules with rasterio's on tessera-eval's
; Austria labels, DIR/austria_crops.geojson (github.com/ucam-eo/tessera-eval),
; and GeoTessera's landmasks, MASKS/<tile>.tiff (github.com/ucam-eo/geotessera,
; from data.source.coop/tessera/tessera). It needs those files and rasterio's
; rasters, which live outside the repository, so no test runs it
; (test/README.md, rasterio/):
;   parity.exe project DIR   writes DIR/jord_*.npy, the labels in UTM 33N;
;   (rasterio, outside the repository, writes DIR/<tile>.* from them);
;   parity.exe compare DIR MASKS   prints the cells where the owners differ,
;     on the grids of the landmasks MASKS/<tile>.tiff, read by Nx_io.load_tiff;
;   parity.exe landmask FILE...    prints each landmask's grid, system, nodata
;     and land cells.

(executable
 (name parity)
 (libraries jord jord.geotiff jord.geojson nx nx.io jsont jsont.bytesrw))
